["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SimpleLicensing/customIdToUri", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "**DEPRECATED in SPDX 3.1.**\nUse [customIdToLicense](./customIdToLicense.md) instead.\n\nMaps a LicenseRef or AdditionRef string for a Custom License or a Custom\nLicense Addition to its URI ID.\n\n**NOTE:**\nThis property is deprecated and only included for backward compatibility.\nNew documents should use [customIdToLicense](./customIdToLicense.md) instead.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/module", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/requirementUUID", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The UUID used by a requirements management or any other lifecycle management tool to uniquely identify a requirement item. UUID, or universally unique ID, is a standard term in requirements engineering.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/rationale", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A rationale is supporting information that provides the underlying\njustification or reasoning for an associated element, decision, or process.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SbomType/build", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SbomType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/glue", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[GLobal Unique Enterprise (GLUE) Identifiers](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-spice-glue-id/), as defined by the IETF Internet-Draft, is expressed as a GLUE URI, a Uniform Resource Identifier that standardizes the representation of existing organizational entity identifiers.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isci", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "International Standard Collection Identifier (ISCI) is a variable-length identifier standardized by [ISO 27730](https://www.iso.org/standard/44293.html) for identifying collections held by libraries, archives, museums, and other memory institutions. It consists of two parts: the identifier for the assigning organization (an ISIL) enclosed in square brackets, followed by a local collection identifier string (e.g., `[FR-751041001]Casadesus1`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
